1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:05,480
We're looking at loops we've looked at for loops we've looked at while loops.

2
00:00:05,480 --> 00:00:10,960
But we want to illustrate the difference between a four and a while, because they can appear to be

3
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:11,520
the same.

4
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:18,200
As we said, a for loop goes from one number to another number in a range, and it's predefined and

5
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:22,880
preset, whereas a while loop can look like it's doing the same thing, it's going to continue until

6
00:00:22,880 --> 00:00:24,160
a certain condition is true.

7
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:26,280
So it can emulate a for loop.

8
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:31,160
But it is also very useful because you can use it to make a loop.

9
00:00:31,160 --> 00:00:35,520
Continue until something happens when you don't know how long it's going to take.

10
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:37,880
So it's not going to be a set number of iterations.

11
00:00:37,880 --> 00:00:43,320
It could be anything from zero, one to or 1000 iterations until some condition is true.

12
00:00:43,360 --> 00:00:44,400
So we'll see that happen.

13
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:45,640
In this example.

14
00:00:45,840 --> 00:00:52,520
What we are going to be looking at in this example is, is going to be a list of what is in your makeup

15
00:00:52,520 --> 00:00:52,960
bag.

16
00:00:53,080 --> 00:00:55,120
Now this could vary from person to person.

17
00:00:55,120 --> 00:00:59,800
So this program is going to do is it's going to ask the user what is in your makeup bag.

18
00:01:00,040 --> 00:01:05,890
Then the user is going to type it in okay I have some mascara and then click enter.

19
00:01:05,890 --> 00:01:09,010
And again it's going to ask you again what is in your makeup bag.

20
00:01:09,010 --> 00:01:15,250
And the user is going to keep on typing in what is in their makeup bag until they have nothing left.

21
00:01:15,570 --> 00:01:20,570
And obviously it depends, you know, because my makeup bag has got like nothing in it, whereas someone

22
00:01:20,570 --> 00:01:23,210
else's makeup bag may have a whole lot more items in it.

23
00:01:23,210 --> 00:01:27,410
So that's why this is a great example of using the while loop, because we actually don't know how many

24
00:01:27,410 --> 00:01:29,170
items are in your makeup bag.

25
00:01:29,210 --> 00:01:33,090
It's up to you until a certain condition is found to be true, in which case we're going to use the

26
00:01:33,090 --> 00:01:36,690
word done to indicate that I'm done with what's in the makeup bag.

27
00:01:36,810 --> 00:01:38,650
So let's see how that is going to look.

28
00:01:38,650 --> 00:01:43,130
So we're going to write our while we're going to use the variable r while R.

29
00:01:43,130 --> 00:01:45,690
And we want to say is not equal to.

30
00:01:46,210 --> 00:01:47,690
If you remember that's how we write.

31
